  "result": "`src/config/nav.ts` defines the nav trees (`SIDEBAR_NAV`, `SETTINGS_NAV`) and the `visibleNav()` function, which is explicitly documented as \"the only place that decides what a given actor sees\" — it filters each `NavItem` by calling `can(actor, item.action, ...)` from `src/lib/permissions.ts` (role/permission gating, e.g. admin vs viewer) and by checking `item.flag` against the `FeatureFlagSnapshot` via `flagAllows()`/`isEnabled()` from `src/lib/feature-flags.ts` (plan-gated features). `src/components/domain/nav/app-sidebar.tsx` merely calls `visibleNav(SIDEBAR_NAV, actor, flags)` and `visibleNav(SETTINGS_NAV, actor, flags)` to render the result — it doesn't itself decide inclusion/exclusion.\n\nANSWER: src/config/nav.ts",
